erability locus for bipolar affective disorder on chromosome 21q22.3' NATURE GENETICS, vol. 8, 1994, pages 291 - 296, XP002924562</text><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit> <nplcit status="new"><text>N. SHIMIZU ET AL.: 'Transcriptional mapping and genomic sequencing of the Down syndrome critical region of human chromosome21' CYTOGENET CELL GENET., vol. 79, 1997, pages 44 - 45, XP002924567</text><sources><source category="Y"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>NOBUYOSHI SHIMIZU ET AL.: 'Molecular Cloning of a Novel Putative Ca2+ Channel Protein (TRPC7) Highly Expressed in Brain' GENOMICS, vol. 54, 1998, pages 124 - 131, XP002924565</text><sources><source category="XP" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </nplcit> <nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1048727A1</text> <sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>T. FURUSHO ET AL.: 'Clinical DNA Diagnosis Method (in Japanese)' KANEHARA SHUPPAN K.K. 1995, pages 170 - 177, XP002924563</text><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>EIKEN KAGAKU KABUSHIKI KAISYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAGAMINE KENTARO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU NOBUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>EIKEN KAGAKU KABUSHIKI KAISYA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAMINE, KENTARO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU, NOBUYOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAGAMINE KENTARO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU NOBUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAMINE, KENTARO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU, NOBUYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A novel transmembrane protein gene is isolated and its base sequence is determined. The protein encoded by this gene (TRPC7) has 7 transmembrane regions and has a homology with TRP (Transient Receptor Potential), which suggests that it might have a calcium channel function. Since a number of mutations are observed in patients with periodic psychosis, it is considered that TRPC7 is a gene causative of periodic psychosis.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Dans le cadre de cette invention, on a isolé un gène de protéine transmembranaire et on a déterminé sa séquence de base. La protéine codée par ce gène (TRPC7) comporte 7 régions transmembranaires. En outre, elle présente une certaine homologie avec le potentiel récepteur transitoire (TRP). On en a déduit l'éventualité de la présence d'une fonction de canal calcium. Etant donné qu'on a observé plusieurs mutations chez des patients atteints de psychose périodique, on considère que le TRPC7 est un gène responsable de la psychose périodique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>